  "reason": "The occurrence 'later positions' refers to the set of tokens occurring after the current one in a sequence. While this concept is central to the definition and function of a 'causal attention mask' (which prevents attending to these positions), 'later positions' itself describes a spatial/temporal subset of tokens rather than the mechanism or process of attending to them. Therefore, it does not share the same identity as 'attending to later positions' (the process) or other existing concepts like 'position' (a single location). It is a distinct concept describing a specific group of entities within the sequence."
